{"title":"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Alternate_start_to_solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Alternate start to solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> of a circle has length a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-digit integer (base ten). Reversing the digits gives the length of the perpendicular chord <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. The distance from their intersection point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> to the center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is a positive rational number. Determine the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/7/147785ee8675c6444988fbb32ed5e7bcd15a87db.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw(circle((0,0),4)); draw((-4,0)--(4,0)); draw((-2,-2*sqrt(3))--(-2,2*sqrt(3))); draw((-2.6,0)--(-2.6,0.6)); draw((-2,0.6)--(-2.6,0.6)); dot((0,0)); dot((-2,0)); dot((4,0)); dot((-4,0)); dot((-2,2*sqrt(3))); dot((-2,-2*sqrt(3))); label(&quot;A&quot;,(-4,0),W); label(&quot;B&quot;,(4,0),E); label(&quot;C&quot;,(-2,2*sqrt(3)),NW); label(&quot;D&quot;,(-2,-2*sqrt(3)),SW); label(&quot;H&quot;,(-2,0),SE); label(&quot;O&quot;,(0,0),NE);[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"218\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/4/f141e1c0ec90533ad43022a0778439d88c24a2e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=10x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"112\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/4/454ff5a61adb0dec9b406d817aa9a0335e99db32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=10y+x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"114\" height=\"16\" />. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad2daca542a1f5ebe39a4b172146afa90cf8b1cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CO=\\frac{AB}{2}=\\frac{10x+y}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"176\" height=\"39\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/1/0918d32cd0acf8d229371abc8270ed3f750b597c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CH=\\frac{CD}{2}=\\frac{10y+x}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"175\" height=\"37\" />. Scale up this triangle by 2 to ease the arithmetic. Applying the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/2/db2ab11e3f306f161501e912137f1a426d363365.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2CO$\" width=\"37\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/3/ae3cb32b18937a47390c0cac78101262984fe118.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2OH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/2/ef27f9c4c053b17522bf88bea334a243489200e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2CH$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />, we deduce\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/2/df2e6f18a0704de86aef307253101f4de9b08556.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(2OH)^2=\\left(10x+y\\right)^2-\\left(10y+x\\right)^2=99(x+y)(x-y)\\]\" width=\"424\" height=\"22\" /> \n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/b/e7b315b83c0b7c2f735f66c03cf870a83da077d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OH$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> is a positive rational number and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are integral, the quantity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/a/4aa3d3d2b5fc376d4c6a06bcfd7e0a8733fcc5fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99(x+y)(x-y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"18\" /> must be a perfect square. Hence either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/3/643e1765342cf3807fd7d130ee679b71ecd4789b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/d/d3da9f8c7fe0473fdd6f8597eff61d71fedda430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" /> must be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, but as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are different digits, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/5/b1557b400871e9b6f918e46d16becfb2fe1768e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+0=1 \\leq x+y \\leq 9+9=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"246\" height=\"16\" />, so the only possible multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> itself. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/3/643e1765342cf3807fd7d130ee679b71ecd4789b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" /> cannot be 11, because both must be digits. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/d/d3da9f8c7fe0473fdd6f8597eff61d71fedda430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" /> must equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/3/643e1765342cf3807fd7d130ee679b71ecd4789b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" /> must be a perfect square. The only pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> that satisfies this condition is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/e/ebee47473ccec8899da1f91c8df43315f1fbf37b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6,5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/c/3ecee7297b6edb0c076b55fc076d32c47a3cd273.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{065}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />. (Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/a/8eae4d681b9169434161d04eb11492bcf0d4def9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = 56$\" width=\"71\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/9/79988f113a0601e3338eae6d0cbbcc57963d327a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OH = \\frac{33}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"75\" height=\"37\" />.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Alternate_start_to_solution_1\">Alternate start to solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Alternate start to solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since H is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Power_of_a_Point\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Power of a Point\">Power of a Point</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/3/ed33011a4fe4382eafd2dc5989eada27010cc851.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CH^2=(AH)(BH)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"21\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/7/b87fcd8beae522effc3cd2253e40062b28251e38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH=r-OH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"118\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/5/a8507ede4eae7c7f7dd96873b1c24ab57e721544.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BH=r+OH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"16\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the radius of the circle, we deduce the relation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/1/df1d5324c99fe23eb149ee6c194967fe3e230652.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CH^2=r^2-OH^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/0/760d621c8416ad89f520fbb8d97d3ebeacbd7e37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OH^2=\\left(\\frac{10x+y}{2}\\right)^2-\\left(\\frac{10y+x}{2}\\right)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"283\" height=\"48\" />. Continue as above.\n</p><p>~anduran\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME\" title=\"1983 AIME\">1983 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1983 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1983\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017151900\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.046 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 288/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1435/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 92/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7999/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.974      1 Template:AIME_box\n100.00%   12.974      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2769:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017151900 and revision id 209409. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}